WEBVTT

00:00.520 --> 00:02.810
Now that we've seen
that as we take i

00:02.810 --> 00:06.740
to higher and higher powers,
it cycles between 1, i,

00:06.740 --> 00:11.260
negative 1, negative i, then
back to 1, i, negative 1,

00:11.260 --> 00:12.290
and negative i.

00:12.290 --> 00:14.155
I want to see if we can
tackle some, I guess

00:14.155 --> 00:15.780
you could call them,
trickier problems.

00:15.780 --> 00:17.110
And you might see these surface.

00:17.110 --> 00:18.526
And they're also
kind of fun to do

00:18.526 --> 00:22.180
to realize that you can use
the fact that the powers of i

00:22.180 --> 00:23.320
cycle through these values.

00:23.320 --> 00:25.990
You can use this to really,
on a back of an envelope,

00:25.990 --> 00:29.100
take arbitrarily
high powers of i.

00:29.100 --> 00:31.650
So let's try, just
for fun, let's

00:31.650 --> 00:35.310
see what i to the
100th power is.

00:35.310 --> 00:39.280
And the realization here is
that 100 is a multiple of 4.

00:39.280 --> 00:43.800
So you could say that this
is the same thing as i

00:43.800 --> 00:47.467
to the 4 times 25th power.

00:47.467 --> 00:50.050
And this is the same thing, just
from our exponent properties,

00:50.050 --> 00:55.167
as i to the fourth power
raised to the 25th power.

00:55.167 --> 00:57.000
If you have something
raised to an exponent,

00:57.000 --> 00:59.090
and then that is
raised to an exponent,

00:59.090 --> 01:02.300
that's the same thing as
multiplying the two exponents.

01:02.300 --> 01:04.170
And we know that
i to the fourth,

01:04.170 --> 01:05.420
that's pretty straightforward.

01:05.420 --> 01:07.390
i to the fourth is just 1.

01:07.390 --> 01:09.590
i to the fourth is
1, so this is 1.

01:09.590 --> 01:12.300
So this is equal to
1 to the 25th power,

01:12.300 --> 01:15.910
which is just equal to 1.

01:15.910 --> 01:18.867
So once again, we use this
kind of cycling ability of i

01:18.867 --> 01:20.450
when you take its
powers to figure out

01:20.450 --> 01:22.672
a very high exponent of i.

01:22.672 --> 01:24.880
Now let's say we try something
a little bit stranger.

01:27.730 --> 01:31.200
Let's try i to the 501st power.

01:31.200 --> 01:34.620
Now in this situation, 501,
it's not a multiple of 4.

01:34.620 --> 01:36.310
So you can't just
do that that simply.

01:36.310 --> 01:38.226
But what you could do,
is you could write this

01:38.226 --> 01:41.500
as a product of two
numbers, one that

01:41.500 --> 01:44.140
is i to a multiple
of fourth power.

01:44.140 --> 01:45.580
And then one that isn't.

01:45.580 --> 01:47.050
And so you could rewrite this.

01:47.050 --> 01:50.390
500 is a multiple of 4.

01:50.390 --> 01:56.000
So you could write this as
i to the 500th power times i

01:56.000 --> 01:56.960
to the first power.

01:56.960 --> 01:57.230
Right?

01:57.230 --> 01:58.070
You have the same base.

01:58.070 --> 01:59.840
When you multiply,
you can add exponents.

01:59.840 --> 02:02.960
So this would be i
to the 501st power.

02:02.960 --> 02:05.170
And we know that this
is the same thing

02:05.170 --> 02:07.920
as-- i to the 500th power
is the same thing as i

02:07.920 --> 02:10.050
to the fourth power.

02:10.050 --> 02:11.700
4 times what?

02:11.700 --> 02:14.760
4 times 125 is 500.

02:14.760 --> 02:17.280
So that's this part right
over here. i to the 500th

02:17.280 --> 02:21.510
is the same thing as i to the
fourth to the 125th power.

02:21.510 --> 02:26.150
And then that times
i to the first power.

02:26.150 --> 02:27.800
Well, i to the fourth is 1.

02:27.800 --> 02:31.690
1 to the 125th power
is just going to be 1.

02:31.690 --> 02:33.130
This whole thing is 1.

02:33.130 --> 02:37.140
And so we are just left
with i to the first.

02:37.140 --> 02:39.222
So this is going
to be equal to i.

02:39.222 --> 02:41.430
So it seems like a really
daunting problem, something

02:41.430 --> 02:43.180
that you would have
to sit and do all day,

02:43.180 --> 02:46.090
but you can use this cycling
to realize look, i to the 500th

02:46.090 --> 02:47.620
is just going to be 1.

02:47.620 --> 02:51.690
And so i to the 501th is just
going to be i times that.

02:51.690 --> 02:55.060
So i to any multiple of 4--
let me write this generally.

02:55.060 --> 03:00.450
So if you have i to any multiple
of 4, so this right over here

03:00.450 --> 03:04.030
is-- well, we'll just restrict k
to be non-negative right now. k

03:04.030 --> 03:06.380
is greater than or equal to 0.

03:06.380 --> 03:10.250
So if we have i to any
multiple of 4, right over here,

03:10.250 --> 03:16.130
we are going to get 1, because
this is the same thing as i

03:16.130 --> 03:19.280
to the fourth power
to the k-th power.

03:19.280 --> 03:22.180
And that is the same thing
as 1 to the k-th power,

03:22.180 --> 03:23.960
which is clearly equal to 1.

03:23.960 --> 03:25.510
And if we have
anything else-- if we

03:25.510 --> 03:29.340
have i to the 4k plus 1 power,
i to the 4k plus 2 power,

03:29.340 --> 03:31.640
we can then just do this
technique right over here.

03:31.640 --> 03:33.640
So let's try that with a
few more problems, just

03:33.640 --> 03:35.920
to make it clear that
you can do really,

03:35.920 --> 03:38.200
really arbitrarily crazy things.

03:38.200 --> 03:45.020
So let's take i to
the 7,321st power.

03:45.020 --> 03:47.540
Now, we just have
to figure out this

03:47.540 --> 03:52.940
is going to be some multiple
of 4 plus something else.

03:52.940 --> 03:55.870
So to do that, well, you could
just look at it by sight,

03:55.870 --> 03:58.870
that 7,320 is divisible by 4.

03:58.870 --> 04:00.270
You can verify that by hand.

04:00.270 --> 04:02.160
And then you have
that 1 left over.

04:02.160 --> 04:08.020
And so this is going to
be i to the 7,320 times

04:08.020 --> 04:09.770
i to the first power.

04:09.770 --> 04:12.905
This is a multiple of 4-- this
right here is a multiple of 4--

04:12.905 --> 04:17.240
and I know that because
any 1,000 is multiple of 4,

04:17.240 --> 04:21.209
any 100 is a multiple of 4,
and then 20 is a multiple of 4.

04:21.209 --> 04:24.497
And so this right over
here will simplify to 1.

04:24.497 --> 04:26.080
Sorry, that's not i
to the i-th power.

04:26.080 --> 04:28.960
This is i to the first power.

04:28.960 --> 04:33.240
7,321 is 7,320 plus 1.

04:33.240 --> 04:37.287
And so this part right over
here is going to simplify to 1,

04:37.287 --> 04:38.870
and we're just going
to be left with i

04:38.870 --> 04:41.100
to the first power, or just i.

04:41.100 --> 04:42.600
Let's do another one.

04:42.600 --> 04:50.860
i to the 90-- let me try
something interesting.

04:54.030 --> 04:56.230
i to the 99th power.

04:56.230 --> 04:58.860
So once again, what's
the highest multiple

04:58.860 --> 05:01.490
of 4 that is less than 99?

05:01.490 --> 05:02.590
It is 96.

05:05.230 --> 05:08.930
So this is the same thing
as i to the 96th power times

05:08.930 --> 05:11.400
i to the third power, right?

05:11.400 --> 05:14.320
If you multiply these, same
base, add the exponent,

05:14.320 --> 05:16.840
you would get i
to the 99th power.

05:16.840 --> 05:20.410
i to the 96th power, since
this is a multiple of 4,

05:20.410 --> 05:23.740
this is i to the fourth, and
then that to the 16th power.

05:23.740 --> 05:26.850
So that's just 1 to the
16th, so this is just 1.

05:26.850 --> 05:29.670
And then you're just left
with i to the third power.

05:29.670 --> 05:32.940
And you could either remember
that i to the third power

05:32.940 --> 05:35.630
is equal to-- you
can just remember

05:35.630 --> 05:36.880
that it's equal to negative i.

05:36.880 --> 05:39.270
Or if you forget that,
you could just say, look,

05:39.270 --> 05:42.480
this is the same thing
as i squared times i.

05:42.480 --> 05:45.360
This is equal to
i squared times i.

05:45.360 --> 05:48.800
i squared, by definition,
is equal to negative 1.

05:48.800 --> 05:55.340
So you have negative 1 times
i is equal to negative i.

05:55.340 --> 05:58.890
Let me do one more
just for the fun of it.

05:58.890 --> 06:01.840
Let's take i to the 38th power.

06:01.840 --> 06:03.450
Well, once again,
this is equal to i

06:03.450 --> 06:07.230
to the 36th times i squared.

06:07.230 --> 06:09.040
I'm doing i to the 36th
power, since that's

06:09.040 --> 06:11.920
the largest multiple
of 4 that goes into 38.

06:11.920 --> 06:13.730
What's left over is this 2.

06:13.730 --> 06:15.870
This simplifies
to 1, and I'm just

06:15.870 --> 06:20.530
left with i squared, which
is equal to negative 1.
